      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COBERLY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Judicial discretion is not a whim. It is to be guided by sound legal principles and subject to meaningful appellate review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What is the standard of review that the court of appeals uses for sentence -- for sentences?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "government's position, which is, well, in a sentence reduction, when it's reduced and it falls within the guidelines, the government's position, as I understand it, is essentially that that decision is unreviewable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Does that -- should that be a factor in our decision; i.e., the obvious workload on the federal courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Why would this preclude appellate review? Isn't it pretty obvious what -- or couldn't the court of appeals infer that what the district court did was this:"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What else can you say besides that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in this case, the AO-247 form has a spot on the second page for additional comments."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So -- so let's do a different hypothetical. The judge says: I gave the 114 because he got convicted of a prison in -- infraction that was at the highest level. And, in fact -- not the facts of this case -- the prison infraction was at the lowest level and didn't even result in anything except a warning. How would the appellate court know that the judge made a factual assumption that was erroneous in picking that 114?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, is Taylor just about the statute? In Taylor, is that all it's about? Because, certainly, Taylor seemed to suggest a broader rule. It said, you know, where, as here, Congress has directed a district court to consider particular factors, in order to have effective appellate review, we need some brief statement about why the court has come out the way it has based on those factors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What would be the minimum that would suffice here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-17-5639",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c5dc719aaf31f67d498a7dcc1aa567218f6e2d431de3723ee97263662109a2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c5dc719aaf3-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
